WEBVTT

00:00:11.148 --> 00:00:13.150
Reconfirm Salvage Object location.

00:00:13.943 --> 00:00:17.446
Hinosawa Bio Pharmatech,
class 3-S sample container.

00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:19.782
Level seven, ILS Block.

00:00:20.783 --> 00:00:21.617
Let's go!

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.160
"CONTAMINATION QUARANTINE"

00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:58.320
It hasn't even been three minutes!

00:00:58.404 --> 00:00:59.238
How?

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:06.745
Nice work, Haruka.
Which floor did you send it to?

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:07.913
Hinosawa Pharma.

00:01:07.997 --> 00:01:11.041
There's lots of stuff
the Matter likes over there.

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.418
Let's go get it.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.627
Wilco!

00:01:18.549 --> 00:01:19.675
Hey! What gives?

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:21.635
You guys are here, too?

00:01:22.136 --> 00:01:23.679
You're onto this lab, too?

00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:25.931
The client's route is blocked.

00:01:26.098 --> 00:01:28.600
You could have buried us!

00:01:28.684 --> 00:01:30.185
Your fault. Eyes up!

00:01:30.602 --> 00:01:32.021
Jerk!

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:38.402
Evidence!

00:01:40.696 --> 00:01:42.323
Bravo 29 Gamma!

00:01:47.202 --> 00:01:49.622
Another diver must have sent it our way.

00:01:49.705 --> 00:01:51.332
Another diver team?

00:01:51.415 --> 00:01:53.375
Lots of tenants in this building.

00:01:56.962 --> 00:01:57.963
What the...

00:01:58.047 --> 00:01:58.964
It was you!

00:01:59.048 --> 00:02:00.966
Did you send the Matter our way?

00:02:01.175 --> 00:02:03.469
-You were there?
-Hell yeah!

00:02:03.552 --> 00:02:05.012
I didn't know that.

00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:09.725
You're the ones who brought it
all the way up here.

00:02:09.808 --> 00:02:11.518
You've got some nerve!

00:02:12.102 --> 00:02:16.231
I thought the Malignant Matter
in this area was Bravo class.

00:02:16.315 --> 00:02:17.566
It's supposed to be.

00:02:19.026 --> 00:02:21.320
It's still active after so many shots?

00:02:21.403 --> 00:02:24.531
Something is different
about this one today.

00:02:24.615 --> 00:02:26.992
We're leaving that thing to you.

00:02:27.076 --> 00:02:28.035
Hey!

00:02:30.037 --> 00:02:32.164
Make sure we get the right sample!

00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:33.916
After all this trouble,

00:02:33.999 --> 00:02:36.960
I'll kill myself if we bring
back the wrong one.

00:02:37.544 --> 00:02:40.631
Zero-seven-eight-two.

00:02:41.006 --> 00:02:42.049
There it is!

00:02:42.132 --> 00:02:45.552
Experimental Spinal Material 0782.

00:02:45.636 --> 00:02:48.305
Ready to live it up
overseas for six months?

00:03:22.131 --> 00:03:23.215
I'll make a shortcut!

00:03:23.298 --> 00:03:25.467
Kaede, we're going this way.

00:03:26.844 --> 00:03:27.720
Opening!

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.146
Sagami! Sagami!

00:03:37.229 --> 00:03:38.814
Some things never change.

00:03:38.897 --> 00:03:40.315
You're still an amateur.

00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:44.194
If that was your real arm,
it'd be gone by now, Kazuki.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.220
Aiko! Are you okay?

00:04:10.304 --> 00:04:12.055
-Tachibana!
-Aiko!

00:04:20.564 --> 00:04:22.900
Are you all right, Tachibana?

00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:24.109
Yes.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.238
You've got a bruise!
Who's in charge of first aid?

00:04:28.697 --> 00:04:30.199
I'm fine.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.663
I could have sworn I scraped it.

00:04:37.372 --> 00:04:39.875
It's a good thing you weren't hurt.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.711
I can't believe you fell asleep
during a game.

00:04:42.795 --> 00:04:45.130
I think you're still not ready for PE.

00:04:45.214 --> 00:04:48.300
I've been falling asleep lately
without noticing.

00:04:48.383 --> 00:04:51.303
Even when I'm not tired.
And I have weird dreams.

00:04:51.386 --> 00:04:52.971
Are you sleeping at night?

00:04:54.223 --> 00:04:55.390
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:04:55.474 --> 00:04:57.017
Are you sure?

00:04:57.184 --> 00:04:58.811
You worry too much, Naho.

00:04:58.894 --> 00:05:00.521
Well, if you say so.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.857
I hope you can go back home soon.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.901
Yeah.

00:05:06.777 --> 00:05:08.821
I guess you're right.

00:05:12.825 --> 00:05:14.243
<i>You going to club today?</i>

00:05:14.326 --> 00:05:17.037
<i>I've got a checkup,</i>
<i>so I won't be there.</i>

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.122
<i>Okay, I'll come get you tomorrow.</i>

00:05:19.206 --> 00:05:20.207
<i>Okay.</i>

00:05:26.213 --> 00:05:28.674
-I'm back.
-Welcome back, Tachibana.

00:05:39.851 --> 00:05:42.062
<i>Oh, it's you, Aiko.</i>
<i>Welcome home.</i>

00:05:42.145 --> 00:05:43.146
Hi, Mizuki.

00:05:43.647 --> 00:05:44.982
<i>Were you all right?</i>

00:05:45.065 --> 00:05:47.943
<i>Your vitals had me worried for a second.</i>

00:05:48.026 --> 00:05:49.403
I had a little fall.

00:05:50.779 --> 00:05:52.781
It wasn't a big deal.

00:05:54.032 --> 00:05:56.743
The school contacted me
to say you're okay,

00:05:57.077 --> 00:05:58.287
but be more careful.

00:05:58.495 --> 00:05:59.621
Sorry, I will.

00:05:59.788 --> 00:06:02.082
Have you gotten used to school?

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:05.669
Yes, bit by bit.
There's an old friend of mine there, too.

00:06:06.878 --> 00:06:11.633
It's kind of strange going to a school
on the hospital property.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.303
It's nice.
You can sleep late if you want.

00:06:14.386 --> 00:06:15.804
Yes, that's true.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.321
Your muscles are recovering.

00:06:33.363 --> 00:06:35.866
Good evening, Dr. Isazu.

00:06:35.949 --> 00:06:38.660
You'll be walking normally in no time.

00:06:39.119 --> 00:06:41.163
You had some slight nerve damage.

00:06:41.538 --> 00:06:44.207
It may feel strange
until you get used to it.

00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:46.418
Have you had any problems?

00:06:48.587 --> 00:06:51.465
-No.
-Feel free to tell me anything.

00:06:52.049 --> 00:06:56.094
You see, we're taking on the role
of your parents for you now.

00:06:57.971 --> 00:06:59.014
Thank you.

00:07:25.123 --> 00:07:28.377
-Oh, God! We're late!
-I had another weird dream.

00:07:28.752 --> 00:07:30.379
Don't tell me about it now!

00:07:41.682 --> 00:07:43.016
Aiko!

00:07:51.483 --> 00:07:52.317
Aiko!

00:07:53.485 --> 00:07:55.487
Are you okay, Aiko? Are you hurt?

00:07:56.405 --> 00:07:57.280
You klutz!

00:07:58.448 --> 00:07:59.658
I'm sorry.

00:08:00.575 --> 00:08:02.828
Hurry up! We'll be late for class!

00:08:05.831 --> 00:08:06.873
Aiko?

00:08:10.502 --> 00:08:12.546
-Come on, Aiko!
-Oh, right!

00:08:17.759 --> 00:08:19.970
I guess it's time to begin.

00:08:20.804 --> 00:08:23.473
Wow! We made it!

00:08:23.557 --> 00:08:27.686
What was that all about?
I've never seen that guy before.

00:08:28.937 --> 00:08:29.813
Aiko?

00:08:33.316 --> 00:08:34.860
-What's wrong?
-What?

00:08:35.444 --> 00:08:38.321
Do you know that guy?
Was it a destined reunion?

00:08:38.905 --> 00:08:40.449
Of course not!

00:08:40.741 --> 00:08:43.201
All right, everyone!
I have big news!

00:08:43.285 --> 00:08:46.329
Even though tomorrow
is the last day of school,

00:08:46.413 --> 00:08:49.124
we have a new transfer student.

00:08:49.249 --> 00:08:52.294
Okay, put on a big smile and come on in!

00:08:56.298 --> 00:08:57.299
It's that guy!

00:08:58.425 --> 00:09:00.552
This is like a romance novel.

00:09:00.635 --> 00:09:02.345
What's that all about?

00:09:10.771 --> 00:09:12.856
Aiko. You're standing.

00:09:12.939 --> 00:09:14.524
-What?
-What?

00:09:26.078 --> 00:09:27.079
Yuya Kanzaki

00:09:27.162 --> 00:09:29.247
You think that guy's a Burster?

00:09:29.331 --> 00:09:31.541
Hey, is he your friend?

00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:34.002
-How do you know him?
-A destined reunion?

00:09:34.586 --> 00:09:35.712
It's not like that.

00:09:35.879 --> 00:09:38.090
We just ran into him downstairs.

00:09:38.173 --> 00:09:40.550
Why'd you transfer so late in the year?

00:09:41.384 --> 00:09:43.595
I go to Kiryu Hospital
for tests tomorrow.

00:09:43.845 --> 00:09:45.138
-Oh.
-Were you hurt?

00:09:45.222 --> 00:09:48.100
-Best of luck.
-He must be a Burster.

00:09:56.983 --> 00:09:58.819
What are you doing, new guy?

00:09:59.402 --> 00:10:01.113
-What are <i>you</i> doing?
-Club stuff.

00:10:01.363 --> 00:10:03.031
Here it goes!

00:10:03.657 --> 00:10:05.283
We're in the Paper Plane Club.

00:10:05.408 --> 00:10:07.244
Paper Plane Club?

00:10:08.995 --> 00:10:11.164
Wow, it's really flying far.

00:10:11.998 --> 00:10:12.916
Want to try?

00:10:17.546 --> 00:10:18.797
This is well-made.

00:10:19.131 --> 00:10:21.091
So, you're interested in paper airplanes.

00:10:21.341 --> 00:10:23.176
Why don't you join our club?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.845
Shimada! You're next!

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.972
I'm coming!

00:10:30.267 --> 00:10:31.309
Hey!

00:10:32.769 --> 00:10:35.480
It's okay. I stood up earlier.

00:10:36.273 --> 00:10:38.441
You're staying at the hospital, too?

00:10:38.567 --> 00:10:39.401
What?

00:10:39.651 --> 00:10:41.027
For your tests.

00:10:41.778 --> 00:10:42.737
Yes.

00:10:44.656 --> 00:10:45.657
Are you a Burster?

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:50.954
So...

00:10:52.497 --> 00:10:56.126
I'm surprised something
so delicate flies well outside.

00:10:56.793 --> 00:10:58.628
There's a chip inside.

00:10:59.129 --> 00:11:00.338
We can track it.

00:11:00.714 --> 00:11:02.799
Do you like paper planes?

00:11:03.174 --> 00:11:07.095
Well, actually, this was supposed to be
the origami club.

00:11:07.304 --> 00:11:08.305
Origami?

00:11:08.763 --> 00:11:11.975
It was part of my
rehabilitation in the hospital.

00:11:12.225 --> 00:11:14.477
That's why I joined this club.

00:11:14.895 --> 00:11:17.647
But somehow
we got hooked on paper planes.

00:11:19.107 --> 00:11:20.525
Next! Tachibana!

00:11:21.776 --> 00:11:22.652
Okay!

00:11:25.739 --> 00:11:26.907
I hope it goes far.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.658
Go for it, Aiko!

00:11:30.785 --> 00:11:31.745
It feels great!

00:11:33.038 --> 00:11:34.414
When you say far...

00:11:36.416 --> 00:11:38.835
Like to the Border Zone?

00:11:39.336 --> 00:11:40.253
I doubt that.

00:11:40.337 --> 00:11:43.882
Besides, I won't be able to get it back
if it goes <i>that</i> far.

00:11:45.634 --> 00:11:47.844
Your name is Kanzaki, right?

00:11:48.386 --> 00:11:49.554
Are you from here?

00:11:49.638 --> 00:11:50.639
Yes.

00:11:51.264 --> 00:11:52.349
I see.

00:11:53.058 --> 00:11:56.353
<i>It sure has changed ever since that day.</i>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.814
<i>The look of the town and the mountains.</i>

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.817
<i>So much has changed in so many ways.</i>

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.529
<i>A Black Box?</i>

00:12:06.613 --> 00:12:07.906
<i>Some are gone.</i>

00:12:08.573 --> 00:12:12.118
Yura was working independently
on Project A.I.C.O.

00:12:12.202 --> 00:12:13.912
He didn't even have a team.

00:12:14.496 --> 00:12:15.497
<i>And Kurose?</i>

00:12:15.789 --> 00:12:18.500
Even he doesn't know the details.

00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:22.462
He died before Yura
could compile the results.

00:12:23.046 --> 00:12:25.882
<i>So, you just want those Yura Notes?</i>

00:12:25.966 --> 00:12:30.178
We can't even be certain they exist.

00:12:32.389 --> 00:12:33.390
Come in.

00:12:33.723 --> 00:12:36.726
I'll contact you if anything else happens.
Goodbye.

00:12:37.727 --> 00:12:39.270
Was that Madam Nanbara?

00:12:39.604 --> 00:12:40.480
What do you want?

00:12:40.563 --> 00:12:45.110
Yes, sir. There's something
I would like to tell you about the school.

00:12:45.694 --> 00:12:47.988
I'm with the hospital, you know.

00:12:48.071 --> 00:12:50.031
I know about that, but...

00:12:50.573 --> 00:12:55.078
something concerns me about
the male student who just transferred in.

00:13:00.291 --> 00:13:01.876
Good morning, Aiko.

00:13:02.961 --> 00:13:04.587
Summer vacation starts tomorrow.

00:13:04.671 --> 00:13:06.006
Yes, it does.

00:13:06.172 --> 00:13:09.592
Now that you can stand on your own,

00:13:09.884 --> 00:13:13.388
why don't you visit home
to pick up some of your things?

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.562
In my heart,

00:13:20.937 --> 00:13:25.233
I still can't believe that
my mother, father, and brother

00:13:25.942 --> 00:13:27.736
are all dead.

00:13:28.862 --> 00:13:31.990
I think that
they just might be alive somewhere.

00:13:32.741 --> 00:13:35.535
But if I go back home

00:13:35.702 --> 00:13:38.413
and see that nobody is there,

00:13:38.872 --> 00:13:42.333
then I won't have any choice but to accept

00:13:43.126 --> 00:13:47.213
that they really are gone.

00:13:48.089 --> 00:13:51.634
They are all alive inside my heart now,

00:13:51.885 --> 00:13:53.762
but they'll disappear if I go.

00:13:55.597 --> 00:13:56.598
Hey.

00:13:58.016 --> 00:13:59.100
Kanzaki!

00:14:00.477 --> 00:14:02.896
If I were your family,

00:14:04.105 --> 00:14:07.650
I'm sure I would feel sad
if you never came home.

00:14:09.527 --> 00:14:10.528
Why?

00:14:13.281 --> 00:14:14.699
I had a family, too.

00:14:21.664 --> 00:14:22.749
I'm going.

00:14:25.001 --> 00:14:28.963
I'll go with you. You must have a lot
to bring back with you.

00:14:29.923 --> 00:14:32.342
You can help us, too, Kanzaki.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.427
Me?

00:15:05.458 --> 00:15:07.252
Say when it's okay to come in.

00:15:07.627 --> 00:15:08.545
Okay.

00:16:11.816 --> 00:16:12.650
"VACATION NOTES"

00:16:12.734 --> 00:16:14.319
These are from my last school.

00:16:20.783 --> 00:16:22.452
Let's give her more time.

00:16:23.119 --> 00:16:23.953
Okay.

00:16:25.747 --> 00:16:28.082
<i>Those two cars</i>
<i>have been there a while.</i>

00:16:33.963 --> 00:16:37.383
I haven't been in Dad's room in years.

00:17:02.909 --> 00:17:04.786
That pose is so corny, Dad.

00:17:08.206 --> 00:17:10.917
Why didn't we spend more time together?

00:17:12.085 --> 00:17:15.672
Why didn't we talk to each other more?

00:17:16.589 --> 00:17:19.092
Why didn't we do more...

00:17:38.778 --> 00:17:40.196
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

00:17:42.282 --> 00:17:43.533
A present?

00:17:45.827 --> 00:17:48.913
It's a sample of my company's new product.

00:17:51.332 --> 00:17:53.710
I'm sure you will love it, Aiko.

00:17:55.962 --> 00:17:57.463
What is this?

00:17:59.841 --> 00:18:01.009
This looks bad!

00:18:03.928 --> 00:18:06.598
I'm going to take a look. You stay here.

00:18:09.809 --> 00:18:10.768
Aiko!

00:18:14.689 --> 00:18:16.316
It seems we're out of time.

00:18:18.818 --> 00:18:19.986
Come with me!

00:18:20.445 --> 00:18:21.946
-What?
-Hurry!

00:18:24.073 --> 00:18:25.783
-What are you--
-The Burst.

00:18:28.202 --> 00:18:30.705
The only person who can end this disaster

00:18:31.873 --> 00:18:33.207
is you.

00:18:34.792 --> 00:18:37.211
-What is--
-People are here to interfere.

00:18:38.087 --> 00:18:39.380
-Let's go.
-What?

00:18:39.714 --> 00:18:42.133
Wait! What?

00:18:42.759 --> 00:18:46.429
Hey, new guy! Where did you go?

00:18:47.388 --> 00:18:49.182
-He disappeared?
-Let's go!

00:18:49.766 --> 00:18:51.517
What are you doing?

00:18:53.561 --> 00:18:57.523
Tachibana, we have a package for you.
Are you here?

00:19:02.362 --> 00:19:04.113
-What's going on?
-Buckle up.

00:19:04.197 --> 00:19:05.031
What?

00:19:09.452 --> 00:19:11.371
What is going on?

00:19:17.168 --> 00:19:18.670
What is this all about?

00:19:21.339 --> 00:19:23.716
-What did you do?
-Turned off your vitals monitor.

00:19:23.925 --> 00:19:25.843
They can track you if it's on.

00:19:34.644 --> 00:19:38.564
The target, Yuya Kanzaki,
has driven off with Aiko Tachibana.

00:19:38.648 --> 00:19:39.774
We're in pursuit.

00:19:49.409 --> 00:19:51.828
Damn! It's the Matter Defense HQ.

00:20:02.463 --> 00:20:06.300
What? The Town? We can't get in there!

00:20:09.137 --> 00:20:11.013
-What's he doing?
-Don't get too close!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.812
We'll get spotted
if we force our way through.

00:20:54.348 --> 00:20:55.308
Over here.

00:21:05.777 --> 00:21:06.861
Welcome.

00:21:07.987 --> 00:21:10.364
Why did you bring me here?

00:21:13.242 --> 00:21:14.952
Have you told her yet?

00:21:15.036 --> 00:21:16.037
No.

00:21:18.372 --> 00:21:19.707
What's this all about?

00:21:20.082 --> 00:21:21.834
Please, calm down and listen.

00:21:23.336 --> 00:21:27.799
That body of yours
is made to look like the original.

00:21:28.674 --> 00:21:29.801
It's a fake.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.471
What do you mean by that?

00:21:33.888 --> 00:21:36.724
We are going to retrieve your real body.

00:21:37.308 --> 00:21:41.020
In return,
we would like to have your fake body.

00:21:41.687 --> 00:21:45.900
With that body,
we're going to put an end to the Burst.

00:21:46.484 --> 00:21:50.404
What is this all about?
What are you talking about?

00:21:50.613 --> 00:21:55.076
Who the heck are you people?
What do you mean that my body is a fake?

00:22:00.915 --> 00:22:02.208
Bear with me.

00:23:57.782 --> 00:23:59.992
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
